    "prediction": "a window is predicted 'attack' when any of the five rules fires (same decision the TrafficAnomalyAgent uses)",
    "metrics": "window-level precision, recall, F1 and false-positive rate on the held-out set; per-class detection rate (benign: false-positive rate) with Wilson 95 % intervals (z = 1.96); per-file summaries; confusion matrix; target_rule_rate = share of a class's windows on which the rule designated for that class fired",
    "confidence_intervals": "percentile bootstrap over held-out windows, 1000 resamples with replacement, seed 0, 2.5/97.5 percentiles (resamples with an undefined metric are dropped and counted in valid_resamples); Wilson score intervals for proportions; no scipy",
    "baselines": "majority class of the development split; mean Rate > 99th percentile of benign development windows; mean Tot size outside the 1st-99th percentile band of benign development windows",
    "single_evaluation": "the held-out set is evaluated once, after all thresholds and baselines are fixed on the development set"
